/**
 * @defgroup RoModular_Repositories_CPSTL CPSTL
 * @ingroup RoModular_Repositories
 * @brief Portable std vocabulary: containers, strings, functional, traits and algorithms.
 *
 * | Field | Value |
 * | ----- | ----- |
 * | Role | The `std` interface (`cpstd::vector`, `string`, `stack`, `queue`, `function`, type traits, iterators, algorithms) on targets with or without a C++ standard library |
 * | Status | Version `1.1.0` rescue in progress; no tagged release yet |
 * | Source | [ChecheRomo96/CPSTL](https://github.com/ChecheRomo96/CPSTL) |
 * | Runtime dependencies | None |
 * | Build infrastructure | RoModularBuild `v0.4.0` |
 * | Public CMake target | `CPSTL::CPSTL` |
 *
 * CPSTL is the bottom of the planned dependency chain
 * `CPSTL <- Foundation <- (DspCore, MCC) <- MIDILAR`. With `CPSTL_USING_STL`
 * every `cpstd` name is an alias of its `std` counterpart; on targets without
 * a C++ standard library, such as AVR, CPSTL provides its own C++11
 * implementation that never throws. Foundation is planned to build on CPSTL
 * for its `std` vocabulary instead of reimplementing `std` types. Until its
 * first tag this portal does not advertise a CPSTL release. The repository's
 * own README and changelog are authoritative for its API, configuration and
 * validation evidence.
 */
